<!-- COUPLES — white -->
<section id="couples" class="tw-section-white tw-gold-border-bottom">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center g-5">
      <div class="col-lg-6 tw-fade">
        <span class="tw-section-label">For You and Your Partner</span>
        <div class="d-flex align-items-baseline gap-3 mb-1 flex-wrap">
          <h2>Couples Therapy</h2>
          <span style="font-family:var(--ff-heading);font-size:2rem;color:var(--tw-gold);font-weight:600;">$250</span>
        </div>
        <p style="color:var(--tw-gold);font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">50 minutes, in-person or virtual</p>
        <hr class="tw-divider tw-divider-left">
        <p>Every relationship has seasons. Some seasons are warm and connected. Others feel cold, distant, or filled with the same arguments cycling endlessly without resolution. Couples therapy at Twish is not about assigning blame or determining who is right. It is about understanding what is happening between you, and building a stronger, more trusting foundation together.</p>
        <p>Shimul uses Emotionally Focused Couples Therapy (EFCT) as her primary framework for couples work. EFCT is one of the most thoroughly researched and effective approaches to relationship therapy available. It works by helping couples identify the negative interaction cycles that keep them stuck, understand the deeper emotional needs and attachment fears driving those cycles, and then actively reshape the way they connect and communicate.</p>
        <p>Twish welcomes all couples regardless of relationship structure, orientation, or cultural background. Intercultural relationships, same-sex couples, and couples navigating significant life changes such as parenthood, loss, or relocation are all warmly welcomed. Shimul brings deep sensitivity to the unique pressures that different relationship dynamics can create.</p>
        <p>Common areas of focus in couples therapy include communication breakdown, trust and betrayal, emotional distance, intimacy, conflict resolution, cultural or family pressures on the relationship, and navigating major life transitions as a couple.</p>
        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-3 mb-4">
          <span class="tw-badge">Communication</span><span class="tw-badge">Trust Rebuilding</span><span class="tw-badge">Intimacy</span><span class="tw-badge">Intercultural</span><span class="tw-badge">LGBTQ+ Affirming</span><span class="tw-badge">Conflict</span>
        </div>
        <a href="https://twishcare.myndweb.app/shimul/booking" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-tw-primary">Book a Session</a>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-6 tw-fade tw-fade-delay-2">
        <img src="/images/shimul-couples-therapy.png" alt="Couples therapy Mississauga Markham Ontario" class="tw-founder-img">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

